 dict(id=469,slug='ecology-nonnative-versus-invasive',title='A new arrival',hook='A label about origin answers one question, not every question.',q='A species is living outside its native range. Does that fact alone establish that it is invasive and harmful?',options=['No, impacts need evidence','Yes, every non-native species is harmful','Yes, origin alone measures its impact'],answer=0,explain='The first panel records location outside a native range; the second highlights the separate question of impact. A non-native species is not automatically shown to be invasive merely by its origin. Definitions and impacts need context and evidence.',recallq='An introduced plant has not yet been studied for its impact. Can its harmfulness be concluded from introduction alone?',recalloptions=['No','Yes, it must be harmful','Yes, its impact is already measured'],recallwhy='Being introduced does not by itself establish an impact.',left=bird(48,60)+'<path d="M76 60 H123 M111 50 L123 60 L111 70" stroke="#7aa3b3" strokeWidth="3" fill="none"/><text x="75" y="105" textAnchor="middle" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="12">Outside native range</text>',right=bird(48,60)+'<path d="M91 32 Q122 26 125 53 Q127 78 99 81 Q82 82 80 66 Q77 48 91 32Z" fill="#e3e8df" stroke="#a4b4aa"/><text x="103" y="64" textAnchor="middle" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="20">?</text><text x="75" y="111" textAnchor="middle" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="12">Impact requires study</text>',source='Source lead, not checked: US Fish and Wildlife Service, invasive species, https://www.fws.gov/'),
