 dict(id=490,slug='ecology-wildlife-corridor-toy',title='Two habitat patches',hook='A path can connect places that were separated.',q='In this toy map, animals cannot cross the surrounding barrier. What does adding a habitat corridor between the two patches allow in the model?',options=['A route between the patches','A guarantee every animal uses it','Removal of all threats'],answer=0,explain='The first panel shows two patches separated by a stipulated barrier; the second adds a connecting strip. In this toy map, the strip creates a possible route between patches. Real use and effectiveness depend on the species, corridor design and surrounding landscape.',recallq='Two habitats have no other traversable connection in a toy map. What does a usable link between them add?',recalloptions=['A possible route','Proof every animal will travel','A guarantee of no disease'],recallwhy='A usable corridor adds a possible route but not guaranteed movement.',left='<rect x="10" y="35" width="50" height="60" rx="10" fill="#a9cba5"/><rect x="90" y="35" width="50" height="60" rx="10" fill="#a9cba5"/>'+deer(35,65)+'<text x="75" y="125" textAnchor="middle" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="12">Separated</text>',right='<rect x="10" y="35" width="50" height="60" rx="10" fill="#a9cba5"/><rect x="90" y="35" width="50" height="60" rx="10" fill="#a9cba5"/><rect x="58" y="58" width="34" height="16" fill="#a9cba5"/>'+deer(35,65)+'<text x="75" y="125" textAnchor="middle" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="12">A corridor</text>',source=toy),
